; DNS records for pathtopresidency.com, hosting Path to Presidency on GitHub Pages.
; Import in Cloudflare: your domain -> DNS -> Records -> Import and Export -> Import.
;
; IMPORTANT: in the import dialog, UNTICK "Proxy imported DNS records".
; Every record must be "DNS only" (grey cloud) or GitHub can't issue the free
; HTTPS certificate. After importing, check each record shows a grey cloud and
; switch any orange (Proxied) ones to DNS only.

$ORIGIN pathtopresidency.com.
$TTL 3600

; Apex domain -> GitHub Pages (IPv4)
@      IN  A      185.199.108.153   ; cf_tags=cf-proxied:false
@      IN  A      185.199.109.153   ; cf_tags=cf-proxied:false
@      IN  A      185.199.110.153   ; cf_tags=cf-proxied:false
@      IN  A      185.199.111.153   ; cf_tags=cf-proxied:false

; Apex domain -> GitHub Pages (IPv6)
@      IN  AAAA   2606:50c0:8000::153   ; cf_tags=cf-proxied:false
@      IN  AAAA   2606:50c0:8001::153   ; cf_tags=cf-proxied:false
@      IN  AAAA   2606:50c0:8002::153   ; cf_tags=cf-proxied:false
@      IN  AAAA   2606:50c0:8003::153   ; cf_tags=cf-proxied:false

; www.pathtopresidency.com -> GitHub Pages (GitHub redirects it to pathtopresidency.com)
www    IN  CNAME  tylernelsonn.github.io.   ; cf_tags=cf-proxied:false

; Domain verification (recommended). GitHub shows you this record under
; github.com -> Settings -> Pages -> Add a domain. Fill in its value, then
; remove the leading ";" so the record is imported. You can also add it by
; hand in Cloudflare after GitHub gives you the value.
;_github-pages-challenge-tylernelsonn   IN  TXT  "PASTE-THE-CODE-GITHUB-GIVES-YOU"
